<title>SOUTH KOREA: SKorea Hanjin Shipping 96 net plummets.</title>
<headline>SKorea Hanjin Shipping 96 net plummets.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>	  (in billion won unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (won)				   764  vs 5,685</p>
<p>    Net					  8.99  vs 56.87</p>
<p>    Profit before tax		     11.32  vs 75.09</p>
<p>    Revenue				2,051.69  vs 1,916.07</p>
<p>    Dividend (pct, par 5,000 won)</p>
<p>	  common shares			nil   vs   3</p>
<p>    Extraordinary gain		     0.98  vs   1.27</p>
<p>NOTE: Hanjin Shipping, a unit of the Hanjin Group said its share capital in 1996 rose to 11,759,105 from 11,458,109 in 1995 because of convertible bonds. The sharp fall in the net profit was due to a shrinking global shipping market and the weakening won which raised business costs. The extraordinary gain was made from selling used containers.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5648</p>
</text>
